---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Lab Note: NoseFrida and Grownsy First Reset Notes | QuietBabyGear";
const description = "First QuietBabyGear lab note comparing NoseFrida and Grownsy cleanup reset friction, sound, and parent handling notes.";
const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  headline: "Lab Note: NoseFrida and Grownsy First Reset Notes",
  description,
  datePublished: "2026-06-04",
  dateModified: "2026-06-19",
  author: {
    "@type": "Organization",
    name: "QuietBabyGear"
  },
  mainEntityOfPage: "https://quietbabygear.com/lab-notes/nosefrida-grownsy-first-reset-notes/"
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Lab Note</p>
    <h1>NoseFrida and Grownsy first reset notes</h1>
    <p class="lead">This note records our first manual-vs-electric nasal aspirator observations before they are turned into a larger comparison article.</p>

    <h2>Products checked</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Frida Baby NoseFrida manual nasal aspirator</li>
      <li>Grownsy Electric Nasal Aspirator</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Raw reset notes</h2>
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Observation</th>
          <th>NoseFrida</th>
          <th>Grownsy</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Cleaning reset time</td>
          <td>About 60-90 seconds</td>
          <td>About 120-180 seconds</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Parts friction</td>
          <td>Three-part structure, quick to handle</td>
          <td>More parts plus chamber and device-body cautions</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Sound</td>
          <td>Silent, no motor</td>
          <td>SP-1 checked at about 46 dB with a phone meter</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Main parent friction</td>
          <td>Mouth-suction hesitation and disposable filters</td>
          <td>Cleaning caution, charging, vibration, and limited power on hard dried mucus</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>What surprised us</h2>
    <p>NoseFrida's strongest advantage was not just silence. It was control: the parent can adjust suction instantly and strongly. Grownsy's strongest advantage was emotional convenience: pressing a button is easier to start than mouth suction, and the light/music features may help distract a resistant baby.</p>

    <h2>What needs a follow-up</h2>
    <p>We still need a cleaner repeated timing protocol and a higher-setting sound check for Grownsy. The first SP-1 note is useful, but it does not describe the highest suction mode.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
